Z||000021||FieroLisa||02-08-2001||10:33 PM||||sqoach: thats the coupe, which is now sold, but here's how i did it. bought purple wire covers, which i got from a company that had a booth at carlisle show last year, but summit racing sells them too. rewrapped a lot of wires with new high heat tape (summit racing yet again), the gold is a high heat gold paint that i bought at auto zone. i just took the air filter housing off, sanded it, primed it, and sprayed it gold.  that's about it! <BR>oh yah and i had a fiero magnet on the air filter housing, a fiero oil cap sticker and purple spark plug wires from taylor (summit racing sells)<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroLisa (edited 02-08-2001).]||||reg||1
